  "definition": {
   "definition": "Reserve money, also called base money or high-powered money, is the highly liquid component of the money stock and broadly reflects the total monetary liabilities of the Reserve Bank; monetary policy actions that change the size of RBI's balance sheet change reserve money. By RBI's definition, Reserve money = currency in circulation + bankers' deposits with the RBI + 'other' deposits with the RBI. Bankers' deposits are banks' current-account balances with RBI held mainly for the Cash Reserve Ratio and as working funds for clearing. It is published weekly in the WSS (item 7).",
